  scope:"project",
  project:"marketing-api",
  topic_key:"review/nutri-fidelity-534af86",
  content:"**What**: Review of commit 534af86 found the Nutri template recognizes only literal Facebook/Instagram/TikTok-like platform keys, while the production payload uses connector keys such as `meta_ads`/`meta_organic`; normal rows also prioritize `source_platform` over `source_metrics.publisher_platform`, so real Meta payloads hide the Facebook and Instagram panels and their content. The browser fixture masks this by replacing production keys with handcrafted `facebook` and `instagram` keys and inventing platform narrative objects.\\n**Why**: The review had to verify reference fidelity and actual browser-executed visibility against SDD observations #476/#477/#478 and prior finding #499.\\n**Where**: dashboard/report_templates/nutri.html:43,52; tests/test_dashboard_reporting.py:549-587,689-704\\n**Learned**: A real browser test can still be a false positive when its payload shape is not produced by the application contract. The current no-external-request and contrast checks are also partial: the former is a source substring scan, and the latter checks accent text against the body background rather than every effective background."
});text(JSON.stringify(r));

