  content:"**What**: Static review of commit 7073384 found that Adriana row-based campaign, Pinterest, geography, and product tables read only raw `source_metrics` canonical keys, so supported aliases normalized by `process_api_response` (for example `social_spend`, `unique_clicks`, `views`, and `actions`) can disappear from row-level report output even while summary KPIs remain correct.\n**Why**: The user requested an independent read-only Critical/Important review against base 247cc65; this is an Important fidelity gap in the production payload path.\n**Where**: dashboard/report_templates/adriana_hoyos.html:84,89,92,95-96; dashboard/api.py:438-499; dashboard/reporting.py:32-42,151-165; tests/test_dashboard_reporting.py:150-171,549-600\n**Learned**: Adriana browser coverage uses numeric strings under canonical metric names, so it does not exercise the already-supported alias contract. A safe resolver must prefer raw canonical/alias values and use normalized top-level fields only when the raw source proves the metric or one of its aliases was supplied, to avoid rendering synthetic zero fields."
